+## Amendment — one identity, one vocabulary, one epistemic shape
+
+The owner's ruling of 2026-09-21 (P-75) directed one amendment against this
+specification alone.
+
+- **POC-REQ-054** gives every subject one identity on every surface and in the
+  machine answer, and governs the per-claim view of the desired, execution and
+  observed states.
+- **POC-REQ-055** requires every relationship to carry a name from
+  RFC1-25's closed table, in a role pair the table assigns it, or a flag
+  saying it is outside that table.
+- **POC-REQ-060** is amended in place to carry one epistemic record shape and
+  the Inferred label.
+
+Inferred enters as a typed landing zone with no production constructor
+(ruling P-75 Q4). This amendment does not make the arm constructible in
+production; that needs its own owner act. Until then no Inferred record,
+including an inferred edge, is produced, so the non-goal above against
+inferred mappings, edges or intent stands unchanged. In
+`CONTRACT-COVERAGE.md` the one signed row the ruling names is preserved
+unedited beside the amendment rows that supersede it, and four Part B2 beliefs
+move to Part A because a requirement now covers one of their consequences.
+The form of the subject identity is not settled here; the implementation
+slice that lands it proposes the form under POC-REQ-054, and RFC6-1's bar on
+a file path as a selection identity still applies.
+
